{"name":"Cotton Puff","hex":"#ffffe7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cotton","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fibrous substance:\n A soft, fibrous, usually white substance consisting of fine hairs, especially the substance around the seeds of a plant of genus Gossypium.\n Any similar soft, fibrous, white substance of fine hairs, of any origin.","A soft, fibrous, usually white substance consisting of fine hairs, especially the substance around the seeds of a plant of genus Gossypium."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of cotton."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cotton"},{"term":"puff","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sharp exhalation of a small amount of breath through the mouth.","The ability to breathe easily while exerting oneself."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To emit smoke, gas, etc., in puffs.","To pant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/puff"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cotton","blocks":[{"text":"Cotton is a soft, fluffy staple fiber that grows in a boll, or protective case, around the seeds of the cotton plants of the genus Gossypium in the mallow family Malvaceae. The fiber is almost pure cellulose and may contain minor percentages of waxes, fats, pectins, and water. Under natural conditions, cotton bolls facilitate the dispersal of the seeds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/CottonPlant.JPG/330px-CottonPlant.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cotton","wikidata":"Q11457"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/BALLS_OF_COTTON_%28ANDHRA_-SOUTH_INDIA%29_READY_FOR_HARVEST.jpg/500px-BALLS_OF_COTTON_%28ANDHRA_-SOUTH_INDIA%29_READY_FOR_HARVEST.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/BALLS_OF_COTTON_%28ANDHRA_-SOUTH_INDIA%29_R